          <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
          <text>
            <paragraph>Follow-up 1 month after medication deprescribing. Patient reports feeling 'much better' with fewer medications. No more confusion about pills. Home health helping with medication administration. Lost 2kg (less mirtazapine). BP better controlled. Mood stable. No falls since discharge. PT helping with home safety. Subdural hematoma stable on repeat imaging. AFib in rate-controlled rhythm (HR 70s-80s). Patient understands increased stroke risk without anticoagulation but prefers current quality of life. No TIA/stroke symptoms to date. Continues to decline dialysis planning. Will monitor renal function closely - currently Cr 2.2, eGFR 29.</paragraph>
          </text>
